y qualified as such.\par \par \pard\sa60 Users are responsible for independently verifying:\par \par \pard\li360\fi-360\sa60\u8226?\tab Receipt amounts.\par \pard\li360\fi-360\sa60\u8226?\tab Invoice totals.\par \pard\li360\fi-360\sa60\u8226?\tab Supplier balances.\par \pard\li360\fi-360\sa60\u8226?\tab Tax calculations.\par \pard\li360\fi-360\sa60\u8226?\tab Financial reports.\par \pard\li360\fi-360\sa60\u8226?\tab Project budgets.\par \pard\li360\fi-360\sa60\u8226?\tab Construction expenses.\par \pard\li360\fi-360\sa60\u8226?\tab Procurement records.\par \pard\li360\fi-360\sa60\u8226?\tab Payment records.\par \pard\li360\fi-360\sa60\u8226?\tab Project progress information.\par \pard\li360\fi-360\sa60\u8226?\tab Engineering and construction calculations.\par \par \pard\sa60 The developer does not guarantee that reports or calculations generated by BRED satisfy every accounting, taxation, construction, procurement, or regulatory requirement.\par \par \pard\sa60 Users must independently verify the accuracy and suitability of information before relying on it for official, financial, engineering, or contractual purposes.\par \par \par \pard\sb200\sa100\keepn\cf1\b\fs26 11. Privacy and Personal Information\b0\cf0\fs20\par \par \pard\sa60 BRED may process personal information and business information through local application storage, databases, cloud infrastructure, authentication systems, and integrated third-party services.\par \par \pard\sa60 The collection and processing of personal information must be governed by an applicable Privacy Policy and handled in accordance with relevant privacy and data protection laws.\par \par \pard\sa60 Where applicable, the developer will comply with its responsibilities under the Philippine Data Privacy Act of 2012 (Republic Act No. 10173) and its implementing rules.\par \par \pard\sa60 Users must not upload personal information or confidential records unless they have an appropriate legal basis and authority to do so.\par \par \par